---
import Publisher from '../layouts/Publisher.astro';
import DrawnArt from '../components/DrawnArt.astro';
// Thesis: scale means gaining perspective through accessible stories about human questions.
---
<Publisher title="About Scale of Us" description="A publishing house bringing ideas from thinkers and philosophers into illustrated stories about being human in the age of AI." active="about">
  <section class="about-simple wrap" id="beginning">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT SCALE OF US</p>
      <h1>Being human<br />in the age of AI.</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="about-body">
      <div class="about-copy" id="creator">
        <p>We’re learning to live with AI. We need stories that help us find our bearings: who we are, what matters to us, and how we live together.</p>
        <p>Scale of Us is a publishing house built around those questions. We bring ideas from thinkers and philosophers<sup><a class="about-source-ref" href="#about-source-1" id="about-source-ref-1" role="doc-noteref" aria-label="Source 1: reading behind the first story">1</a></sup> across time into illustrated stories anyone can read.</p>
        <p id="formats">For us, scale means gaining perspective. A boy’s question to a machine can become a question about your own life. Each reading is a chance to see it differently.</p>
        <aside class="about-sources" aria-label="Sources" role="doc-endnotes">
          <ol>
            <li id="about-source-1" tabindex="-1">The reading notes for <em>The Boy Who Tried to Catch the Wind</em> include Alfred Korzybski (<em>Science and Sanity</em>), Martin Buber (<em>I and Thou</em>), Michael Polanyi (<em>The Tacit Dimension</em>), Zhuangzi, Simone Weil (<em>Waiting for God</em>), and T. S. Eliot (<em>Four Quartets</em>). <a href="/read/wind/#grown-ups">See the full reading notes</a>. <a href="#about-source-ref-1" role="doc-backlink" aria-label="Back to source reference 1">↩</a></li>
          </ol>
        </aside>
      </div>
      <DrawnArt name="n09" class="about-inquiry" eager />
    </div>
  </section>
</Publisher>
